    "body":  "## Summary\n\nFirst implementation slice of #269: construct the official CA Skill Compiler v2.1.0 Development Build request from exact immutable Interface Package snapshots already imported and locked by the Studio.\n\n- Implement the Compiler-specific `CA-SKILL-DEPENDENCY-SNAPSHOT\\0v1\\0` digest framing over original file bytes, UTF-8 path ordering and big-endian lengths; keep it distinct from the Studio\u0027s existing lock digest.\n- Reproduce the official Compiler v2.1.0 Development Build request fixture.\n- Build Contract root aliases from exact Skill dependency declarations and transitive edges from each locked `package.json` manifest.\n- Select and verify only the exact Contract-root / transitive Interface Package closure. Unrelated project dependencies (including editor-only Interface Packages, ToolCatalogs and Schema Bundles) do not block a Skill that does not reference them.\n- A declared Contract root or required transitive alias resolving to a non-Interface-Package kind fails with an explicit unsupported-kind diagnostic.\n- Verify the Studio lock digest against original bytes before computing the Compiler digest.\n- Fail closed on missing roots/transitive snapshots, stale or tampered bytes, wrong root Package IDs, duplicate aliases, cycles, version conflicts, unready resolver state and source-only Contracts.\n- Do not infer Owner / Capability trust or include `trustedBuildContext`; Host Admission requirements remain separately owned.\n\n## Scope boundary\n\nThis is only the canonical request / digest builder. It does not switch the Worker/WASM, migrate the project lock, or connect Package Audit / AI Authoring to Development Build; those remain in #269 / #276.\n\nThe current MAS Example roots `mas` (ToolCatalog) and `ca-context` (Schema Bundle) are not formal Compiler Interface Packages. Do not substitute the editor-only `ca-client` package or synthesize manifests. The MAS Example remains BLOCKED / NOT_LINKED until the exact upstream Owner and Host Context Interface Packages are published and pinned.\n\n## Exact-head acceptance\n\nHead: `a542df4dc3c0fac1d31ce182107bad3211568470` (current main `1082b635cfa7ecad16602f37f30e4b988efbc4d3` merged as first parent).\n\n- PR Verify: PASS\n- Native Windows standalone Authoring: PASS\n- IDE Host: PASS\n- Theia Browser Host: PASS\n- Theia Browser-Only Chromium: PASS\n- Pages Chromium build: PASS (deployment is skipped for pull requests by workflow policy)\n\nRegression coverage proves unrelated `ca-client`-like Interface Packages, ToolCatalogs and Schema Bundles are ignored when outside the Contract closure, while a required ToolCatalog / Schema Bundle root is rejected with an explicit unsupported-kind diagnostic.\n\n## Tracking\n\nPart of #269\nPart of #279\n\nNo Host Admission, Runtime Execution, 5GC or Production Qualification is claimed.",
